&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;30 days:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Get up to speed on the current state of the Mk3 design. Spend time with each system owner to understand their architecture, open issues, and key risks. Visit the manufacturing facility and learn the build process and its controls. By day 30, share a short written assessment of the biggest technical gaps and risks you see across the vehicle.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;60 days:&lt;/strong&gt; Take ownership of one or more systems and set the requirements for the design or redesign, including load cases and the standards that apply. Develop a first concept, backed by analysis, and present it internally. Complete a peer review of a colleague’s concept.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;90 days:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Complete the design or redesign of your system and prepare for a formal design review. Work with Reliability and Test engineers to complete a DFMEA and fault tree analysis against the requirements, and define how simulation results will be correlated with test data. In parallel, take part in vehicle commissioning and troubleshooting with the team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
